---@class clickhouse_cloud.click_stack.ClickStackStaticListFilter
---@field type clickhouse_cloud.click_stack.ClickStackStaticListFilterType|string Discriminator. Must be "STATIC_LIST".
---@field name string Display name for the dashboard filter key
---@field options clickhouse_cloud.click_stack.ClickStackStaticListFilterOptionsList The values this filter's dropdown offers. Must be non-empty and free of duplicates.
---@field isBroadcastEnabled? boolean Must be false — there is no expression to broadcast. Omit it and it is false. Allowed values: false.
---@field isVariableEnabled? boolean Must be true if provided, and is true when omitted. Tiles reference the selection as `$variableName`, or with the `$__filter(<expression>, $<variableName>)` and `$__conditionalAll(<condition>, $<variableName>)` macros. The one-argument `$__filter($<variableName>)` form renders the filter's own expression, which this kind of filter does not have, so it reports that the expression must be passed explicitly. Allowed values: true.
---@field variableName? string Token tiles reference this filter's selected value by, as `$variableName`. Must start with a letter and may contain only letters, numbers, and underscores. Defaults to the display name with whitespace replaced by underscores and remaining illegal characters removed, so a variable-enabled filter whose name derives nothing usable must send this field explicitly. Variable names must be unique across a dashboard's variable-enabled filters. Names the variable only, so the field is rejected when isVariableEnabled is not true, and is omitted from responses for such a filter.
---@field minSelections? clickhouse_cloud.click_stack.ClickStackStaticListFilterMinSelections|number Minimum number of values that must be selected before tiles load. Set to 1 to make the filter required. Only 0 and 1 are accepted. Omit the field (or send 0) for the default optional behavior.
---@field isGlobalRequirement? boolean Widens a required filter's block to every tile on the dashboard. False (the default) blocks only the tiles that read the filter: those referencing its variableName, and those its broadcast applies to. Ignored unless minSelections is 1.
---@field maxSelections? clickhouse_cloud.click_stack.ClickStackStaticListFilterMaxSelections|number Maximum number of values that can be selected at once. Set to 1 to make the filter single-select. Omit the field for the default multi-select behavior.
---@field id string Unique dashboard filter key ID

